GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "FAA795B9A57095EB"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{FDA9F575D4D4704C}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Summary"
     m_sContent "SD01 - Soviet days 1 | A mission series following a Soviet Motor Rifle Company as they begin their tour in Afghanistan between 1982-1983."\
     ""\
     "Enter the blistering sun with 220 Motor Rifle company as they begin the dangerous journey through Afghanistan, Taki province, to relieve their sister company and settle in for the rest of the year."\
     "The convoy has a way to go still untill they reach safety, but who know's what'll happen along the way..."\
     ""\
     "|SUMMARY NOTES|"\
     "• Setup timer: OPFOR - 6min | INDFOR - None."\
     ""\
     "|WIN CONDITION NOTES|"\
     "OPFOR should choose during slotting how many drivers they want in the logistic team. If they wish to go for a Major, Regular, Minor, or Pyrrhic victory, based on the number of URALS that make it to the end point."\
     "• Major: All 6x unarmed Urals."\
     "• Regular: 4x unarmed Urals."\
     "• Minor: 2x unarmed Urals."\
     "- AND atleast 35% of alive players also reach the end point."\
     "• Pyrrhic: No urals reach the end point, but 35% of the remaining company makes it to the end."\
     ""
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{BFF4B5E06C4FC803}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "|PRELIMS|"\
     "• DTL: 04/04/1982,15:30, Afghanistan, Taki provience."\
     "• Weather: Clear - Vsability 1km+, no forecast of change."\
     ""\
     "|LORE/BACKGROUND|"\
     "During the Soviet–Afghan War, the 220th Motor Rifle Company has been deployed to Taki Province as part of a routine unit rotation. The company’s task is to relieve a sister formation currently occupying a forward operating base and assume responsibility for the area for the next nine months."\
     "At the time of this operation, 220 Company is assembled at a designated staging location, conducting final preparations before movement. The unit is scheduled to advance as a motorized convoy along a planned route to its destination."\
     "The security situation in the region remains unstable. Mujahideen forces operate throughout the province in decentralized, irregular groups. Their strength, equipment, and intentions are well known, but reliable intelligence on recent activity along the route is limited."\
     "Although the convoy movement is assessed as routine, the environment remains unpredictable. Contact with hostile forces is possible during transit, and the unit must be prepared to react to ambush, harassment, or delays along the route."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{06A1AC8F27DC8091}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "|PRELIMS|"\
     "• DTL: 04/04/1982,15:30, Afghanistan, Taki provience."\
     "• Weather: Clear - Vsability 1km+, no forecast of change."\
     ""\
     "|LORE/BACKGROUND|"\
     "During the Soviet–Afghan War, the 220th Motor Rifle Company has been deployed to Taki Province as part of a routine unit rotation. The company’s task is to relieve a sister formation currently occupying a forward operating base and assume responsibility for the area for the next nine months."\
     "At the time of this operation, 220 Company is assembled at a designated staging location, conducting final preparations before movement. The unit is scheduled to advance as a motorized convoy along a planned route to its destination."\
     "The security situation in the region remains unstable. Mujahideen forces operate throughout the province in decentralized, irregular groups. Their strength, equipment, and intentions are well known, but reliable intelligence on recent activity along the route is limited."\
     "Although the convoy movement is assessed as routine, the environment remains unpredictable. Contact with hostile forces is possible during transit, and the unit must be prepared to react to ambush, harassment, or delays along the route."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{43F3C8D201652524}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "|COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION|"\
     "Composition: We are the deadly and fearless Mujahideen, Racek Cell, formed of 29x pax, mixed equipment and experience but great moral!"\
     ""\
     "Disposition: Our cell is currently located at our safehouses laying low for the green light to step-off, at GRID 028098, west of Nagara."\
     ""\
     "|STRENGTH & CAPABILITIES|"\
     "• Our BMP crew were recently trained by the CIA on how to operate various Soviet Armoured Vehicles."\
     "They have knowledge on the BTR, BRDM, T-55, and T-72, if we can capture one of these then the BMP crew can use it."\
     "• We have 6x pax waiting in reserves if we need reinforcements."\
     "• We have 1x BMP, 1x landrover with a front mounted FN-MAG machine gun and top mounted 50cal machine gun, including 2x PKM mounted UAZs."\
     "• We also have 8x unarmed cars, 2x trucks, 5x motorbikes."\
     ""\
     "|LIMITATIONS & RESTRICTIONS|"\
     "• Only the radio operator and BMP crew have radios."\
     "• We've got an old Soviet AT minefield to the east of Nur we should be careful of."\
     "• Terrain is very steep at parts and will greatly limit heavier and non off roading vehicles."\
     "• We have no supporting units or fires available."\
     ""\
     "|SERVICE & SUPPORT|"\
     "• We have a crate next to the BMP which has 1x 12.7mm NSV scope HMV with 4x 50rnd boxes, 16x AT mines, 20x explosive charges, 10x detonators, 80x sandbags, and backpacks."\
     "It's close enough to the BMP to allow us to transfer items across without having to take them out first."\
     "• BMP has a squad level rearm in the back."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{C33370313BEA2CC3}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "|COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION|"\
     "Composition: We are 3220 Motor Rifle Company of the Soviet Union."\
     "Consisting of 37x pax, 2 BTR platoons, 1 supply platoon, and a tank."\
     ""\
     "Disposition: Our company is currently at our rest stop GRID 003056"\
     "holding and preparing to move off along the route. "\
     ""\
     "|STRENGTH & CAPABILITIES|"\
     "• 1x T-72 tank has been attached to us."\
     "• Each BTR platoon has 3x BTRs and 1x BRDM for HQ."\
     "• Our supply platoon has 1x ZU-23 Ural truck and 1x PKM UAZ"\
     "• No air or fires available."\
     ""\
     "|SERVICE & SUPPORT|"\
     "• We have 1x fuel truck, 2x ammo, 2x repair trucks in the supply platoon we can use for fuel, ammo, repair."\
     "• We have 4x unarmed vehicles other than the above."\
     "• Each BTR has rearm for the squad."\
     "• We have no reinforcements, QRF, or supporting friendly units."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CEA51F319EBFA4A0}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "|COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION|"\
     "Composition: Enemy forces are the Soviet Union, 220 Motor Rifle Company. These Soviet companies number roughly 50x pax, split across three platoons (2x BTR, 1x support & supply), and a COY HQ."\
     "Each Platoon minus the supply has 3x BTRs and 1x BRDM, although the supply platoon typically has some kind of light skinned armed vehicles for protection while in transit. "\
     "Reinforced from the regimental tank battalion by 1x T-72."\
     ""\
     "Disposition:"\
     "Our cell has been assigned to this new in country Motor Rifle Company who's arrived here for their tour over the next 9 months."\
     "They're on route currently through this region so they can link up with their sister company and relieve them. "\
     "Currently stopped at their rest stop, staging to step-off shortly from GRID 003056, proceeding North bound."\
     ""\
     "|STRENGTH & CAPABILITIES|"\
     "• 1x T-72, 6x BTRs,3x BRDMs, 1x ZU-23 Ural, 2x PKM UAZ."\
     "• Organic rearm, repair, and refuel within their company."\
     "• Company level medical team."\
     ""\
     "|LIMITATIONS & RESTRICTIONS|"\
     "• Limited in freedom of movement. Terrain restricts vehicle manvers and confines them to vallies often until later in the route near Nur."\
     "• No local supporting units so a QRF would take to long. Reinforcements are highly doubtful."\
     "• Old Soviet AT minefield near Nur."\
     ""\
     "MLCOA: The convoy will follow their planned route in close formation with tight security, stopping to engage any contact with overwhelming power to force us to retreat."\
     ""\
     "MDCOA: The convoy will deploy infantry screens ahead and around the convoy - more so on the hilltops, to guard forward and either force an early engagement or to force us to withdraw from positions by disrupting us, thus potentially revealing us to fire."\
     "This would allow the vehicles to move far less contested to areas which can be strongpointed and used to re-org and continue from."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{498E7E3EB18D39D0}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "|COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION|"\
     "Composition: Enemy forces are the deadly Mujahideen."\
     "Spread throughout this region of Taki province, enemy fighters are estimated to be upwards of around 500x pax consisting mostly of light infantry, with a mix of light skinned armed vehicles, but also the occasional armoured vehicle such as a BMP or T-55"\
     "Blending into the civilian population and also having garrisoned  cells typically in the mountains."\
     ""\
     "Disposition:"\
     "At the current time there is no known location of enemy fighters."\
     "Althought the settlements such as Mullodost and Nagara are very supportive of the Mujahideen and don't take kindly to our presence."\
     ""\
     "|STRENGTH & CAPABILITIES|"\
     "• A BMP was spotted operating within this area as reported by air assets passing overhead who observed it near Nagara."\
     "The Mujahideen have occasionally been known to use captured Soviet armoured vehicles such as BMPs, T-55s, BTRs, BRDMs, although in very limited numbers. "\
     "They appear to have good knowledge of each vehicles operations as if they've had prior training by someone."\
     "• The ability for the cell to call upon reinforcements quickly is likely."\
     "• The use of mines, IEDs, and UXOs are common practice by enemy forces, the current threat is high risk."\
     "- There is an old soviet AT minefield marked on our map east of Nur."\
     "• Known to use mortars, the current threat is low risk."\
     "• The Mujahideen have total freedom of movement within this region."\
     ""\
     "|LIMITATIONS & RESTRICTIONS|"\
     "• Unable to face us in direct combat. Our numbers and firepower would overwhelm them."\
     "• Old Soviet AT minefield near Nur."\
     ""\
     "MLCOA: Attempt to conduct a deliberate ambush while we're on route using explosive charges and/or mines to cause damage and disorientation, after striking quick with vehicles from established firing positons, before hastily withdrawing to conduct similar effects later."\
     ""\
     "MDCOA: Mujahideen forces manage to isolate us from mutual support and fixing friendly callsigns to a location so they can strike with that spotted BMP."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{F07D875D4D8E6A52}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "|MISSION STATEMENT|"\
     "Our mission is to NEUTRALIZE the Soviet convoy while on route before it can reach it's nearest friendly unit."\
     ""\
     "|EXECUTION|"\
     "We shall push out along the route, setting up firing positions, ambush points, blockades, chokepoints, before the Soviet convoy steps off from their staging location."\
     "End state will see roughly 70% of the convoy destroyed or made ineffective so that their overall convoy becomes neutralized."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{32EA4FBE34365C84}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "|MISSION STATEMENT|"\
     "Our mission is to conduct a CONVOY to the finish point at GRID 008105 where we will stop for the night before carrying on our route tomorrow morning to our sister company and relieve them."\
     ""\
     "|EXECUTION|"\
     "Company has decieded on a route through the hills of NW Taki province, passing through the towns of Mulladost, Gospandi, Nagara, and Nur."\
     "We should reference the waypoint markers along our route."\
     "End state shall be the company rallied at the finish point."\
     "- (We can choose when to end the mission by interacting with the radio on the desk at the route finish - This allows you to wait for stray trucks crawling in for example)"\
     ""\
     "• This is not a route clearence."\
     "Think about using our pax and assets to secure checkpoints along the way, so the next callsigns can pass through safely, a bounding convoy basically."\
     "• We are not strictly fixed to the road. While this is our general route we should follow, we can go off course if need be to avoid contact, obstacles or anything that may hinder us."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{60D43E26DB8C6E89}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "Comsig"
     m_sContent "|CALLSIGNS|"\
     "• HQ - Racek-21"\
     "• BMP - Racek-22"\
     "• MG Team - Racek-23"\
     "• Assault team 1 - Racek-24"\
     "• Assault team 2 Racek-25"\
     ""\
     "|FREQ/CHAN|"\
     "• All callsigns - 40Mhz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CABFC975A109A841}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "Comsig"
     m_sContent "|CALLSIGNS|"\
     "• Tank - 421"\
     "• COY HQ - 220"\
     "• 1 PHQ - 221H"\
     "- 1st BTR - 221"\
     "- 2nd BTR - 222"\
     "- 3rd BTR - 223"\
     "• 2 PHQ - 231H"\
     "- 1st BTR - 231"\
     "- 2nd BTR - 232"\
     "- 3rd BTR - 233"\
     "• 3 PHQ - 241H"\
     "- Logi team - 241"\
     "- ZU23 team - 242"\
     ""\
     "|FREQ/CHAN|"\
     "All callsigns - 48Mhz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{C5B62E03AA0143DF}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "Mission notes"
     m_sContent "|END CONDITIONS|"\
     "USSR:"\
     "• Major win - 6x unarmed Urals reach the end point "\
     "• Regular win - 4x unamred Urals reach the end point."\
     "• Minor win - 2x unarmed Urals reach the end point."\
     "- AND atleast 35% of alive players also reach the end point."\
     "• Pyrrhic win - No urals reach the end point, but 35% of the remaining players makes it to the end."\
     ""\
     "(USSR can call the mission at their finish point by interacting with the radio on the table. This is so they can wait at the FP for trucks to still arrive and choose the end victory type)"\
     ""\
     "Mujahideen:"\
     "• Kill at least 75% of the Soviet company."\
     ""\
     "|MISC|"\
     "• Setup timer: OPFOR - 6min | INDFOR - None."\
     "• Ratio: 2:1"\
     "• Timelimit: None"\
     "• AO limits: Yes - Both teams."\
     ""\
     "Mission created by: TheLocalPub"\
     "Use the #feedback channel on DM me on Discord to provide logged feedback, complaints, etc."\
     ""\
     "|FOOTNOTE|"\
     "This mission is the first in a small series of missions that will follow a Soviet Motor Rifle Company while they conduct their tour for the year in Afghanistan."\
     "Prefixed as \"SD01\" standing for \"Soviet Days\" followed by the mission number; the \"Days\" missions eventually turned into a whole series following other units on their tours through other eras and conflicts."\
     "The mission series was created by ReddishRed back in Arma 3. This is a small gesture to him."
    }
    GC_Briefing "{E30C5B3841932966}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "Changelog"
     m_sContent "Changed: "\
     "• ORBAT of the USSR team. "\
     "Almost all infantry have been removed, drastically lowering playercount. This is to relieve the burden of having just infantry sat in the back of a BTR doing nothing over many miles."\
     "Instead, to make up the firepower, each PLT HQ has a BRDM. So 2x BRDMs added but 6x squads of infantry removed."\
     "• Header config to no longer say 1-88 playercount as this clearly triggered people."\
     "• Mujahideen equipment and supply crate to better aid them in stopping the convoy."\
     "• Updated the briefs."\
     ""\
     "Added:"\
     "• Ambient Civ AI to the towns and roads to increase the ambient feel."\
     "• New heavy weapons to the insurgent side."\
     "• New minefield next to the old one which creates a tight funnel point."\
     "• Extra props around the place and cover to the hills."\
     "• INDFOR now uses the new platoon command unit."\
     ""
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
